":false,"timestamp":1788549787044},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No existing hx-sync. origin/master is f2c0e7b, and merge-base is f2c0e7b, so SHA contains origin/master exactly (origin/master is parent). Good.\n\nNow let me consider whether the race is enough to mark `changes`. I want to make a well-reasoned decision. Let me re-read the system prompt about finding severity: \"Report only problems introduced or exposed by this Revision.\" \"For each finding, give the location, failure mode, impact, evidence, and required remedy. Set severity from demonstrated risk. Do not inflate it.\" And \"Approve only when all required Checks pass and no blocking finding remains.\"\n\nThe race: location `templates/instance.html` (shared `hx-target=\"#log-drawer-body\"` for all log links) and `static/canopy.js` (no request coordination/abort). Failure mode: two log requests in flight to the same swap target; the slower/older response can overwrite the newer selection, so the drawer displays the wrong run's log. Impact: operator may read the wrong log, undermining the feature's purpose. Evidence: all log links target the same element; `handleLogs` can take up to `refreshTimeout` (30s); htmx does not serialize/abort without `hx-sync`; no sequence guard. Required remedy: serialize or abort (e.g., `hx-sync=\"#log-drawer-body:abort\"` or maintain a request token in canopy.js and discard stale responses).\n\nThis is concrete and evidence-backed. I'll mark it as a blocking finding (changes).\n\nAre there any other blocking findings? Let me think about the copy button on direct navigation. Not blocking. I can mention as non-blocking in the summary? The summary for changes should put concrete reasons. I can include the race as the reason and perhaps the minor direct-nav issue as additional context, but keep concise.\n\nWait, before deciding changes, let me consider whether the Verifier is expected to approve this branch if there are no failing checks, and the